        <br>
        Setup:<br>
      </font></p>
    <p style="font-family: Times New Roman,Times,serif;"><font size="-1">We

        will be using the MPCS GitLab server for version control. The
        department has published a tool to replace GitHub's Classroom.
        You will login with your CNET ID at
        https://course-repos.cs.uchicago.edu/. Here you will find
        classes you're registered for that have repositories for that
        class. You will click on the MPCS 51205 — Topics in Software
        Engineering course for which the repository has been created for
        then that should take you to the repository that's been created.
        You can click on your CNETID (as that should have a hyperlink)
        to take you to the GitLab repository page. That page will
        contain the instructions needed to clone your repository. You
        will then perform standard git add, git commit, git push for all
        homework assignments. This will mean you will perform mkdir
        commands to create lab repos, which you will push up to your
        source main branch.<br>
        <br>
        Please reach out if you have any questions or issues.<br>
        <br>
      </font></p>
  </body>
</html>
